  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "performance",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Mixtral and Qwen3 MoE left attention output dtype unspecified, allowing their output projections to produce half precision before addition to the float residual stream.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5f7a3fcce4674726b719bf6d57ff098a",
          "call_0aab7467cd8443a094e93a11259fc3d8",
          "call_6e068bc90e574eb4b7babe46f7cf11d2",
          "call_73e50fd567074ba6ab07dc5e4a842e6c",
          "call_7f978a12f8144486937c55cd55bd3e27",
          "call_6610d781c2e740119a7691e2b91e6344"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Both builders now pass out_dtype=torch.float to Attention. This configures the output projection itself, rather than merely widening its already-rounded result.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5c16deae6ae445e8a7386327c03db93f",
          "call_02d033cbadc1421b872239568f839e66",
          "call_41d70a88653d4ded9feb7a3951b9ad5f"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "The change avoids a half-precision output boundary before residual addition, but also enlarges that temporary output and can change numerical results. A net speedup is not established.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_73e50fd567074ba6ab07dc5e4a842e6c",
          "call_7f978a12f8144486937c55cd55bd3e27",
          "call_6610d781c2e740119a7691e2b91e6344",
          "call_7f377b867d7f4ac18d275e825068d628"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The introducing Mixtral and Qwen3 MoE entries describe assembly from shared attention and sparse-expert modules. The Qwen3 entry also records a conditional all-expert fused-buffer mismatch.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_45ac30cbc09345ce8f06aa6ec3bc0a6a",
          "call_bc5db840ae2641a8a7015046fcba68e8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The component-refactor entry records Qwen3MoeConfig supplying a bare class instead of a component dictionary. That old form is absent in the inspected parent: Qwen3MoeConfig already supplies {\"text\": Qwen3MoeModel}, which this diff leaves unchanged.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_e1246af5b2384cd9ac9d848ca8324230",
          "call_0aab7467cd8443a094e93a11259fc3d8",
          "call_02d033cbadc1421b872239568f839e66"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #35, \u201chumaneval.py: fix top_k type, remove rep_p, add qwen3,\u201d concerns evaluation and sampling; issue #29, \u201cAuto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?\u201d, concerns scaling policy. Their association here is inference from shared Qwen3 terminology, not evidence motivating this dtype change. Issue #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant,\u201d reports a Cholesky failure; its inferred association is the inspected linear.py conversion call appearing in its traceback, not a demonstrated connection to attention output precision.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
