    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Keep attention output in float through residual addition",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The two edits apply the same existing option independently to every constructed attention layer. Attention stores out_dtype and passes it to o_proj only; Q/K/V projections retain their existing precision. All three attention backends converge on project_o, and Attention.forward applies the requested output dtype through to2.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5c16deae6ae445e8a7386327c03db93f",
              "call_02d033cbadc1421b872239568f839e66",
              "call_41d70a88653d4ded9feb7a3951b9ad5f",
              "call_64df0f146f1a4107815092ae78ea756d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Linear propagates the stored dtype when loading FP16 or EXL3 weights and when converting to EXL3. LinearFP16 allocates the requested output: with half input and float output it selects ext.hgemm instead of torch.matmul. The native function requires two-dimensional half inputs and compatible shapes, and uses cublasGemmEx with float output and CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32F.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_dd3452e6a17e4075b2b6da089f2eb331",
              "call_7f978a12f8144486937c55cd55bd3e27",
              "call_d7e486cee6bf4f75b18bade4a6a53f43"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "LinearEXL3 likewise allocates y using the stored output dtype. Both its reconstruction route and direct EXL3 route receive that buffer. The native EXL3 entry accepts float or half output while retaining half input; the patch does not change its token-count dispatch or weight representation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6610d781c2e740119a7691e2b91e6344",
              "call_ab061c985de64359a1eb8843744137c8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inspected direct attention callers are TransformerBlock.forward and ParallelDecoderBlock.forward; neither overrides output dtype. These two models use TransformerBlock, whose embedding-origin residual is float and whose attention result is added in place. The subsequent MLP normalization still explicitly produces half precision. Mixtral's half MoE output and Qwen3 MoE's float MoE output are unchanged, as is the half final normalization.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5bdd464bafe1499985ce608e231a40f9",
              "call_73e50fd567074ba6ab07dc5e4a842e6c",
              "call_6e068bc90e574eb4b7babe46f7cf11d2",
              "call_5f7a3fcce4674726b719bf6d57ff098a",
              "call_0aab7467cd8443a094e93a11259fc3d8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library scalar illustration rounded a float projection value of 1.000100016593933 through half before adding a residual of 1: the result was 2.0, versus 2.0001001358032227 without the half boundary. Packed half and float sizes were two and four bytes. This demonstrates possible rounding and storage differences, not actual model outputs or GPU speed.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7f377b867d7f4ac18d275e825068d628"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All four inspected Mixtral configurations\u2014mistralai/Mixtral-8x7B-v0.1, Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1, Mixtral-8x22B-v0.1 and Mixtral-8x22B-Instruct-v0.1\u2014declare MixtralForCausalLM. Each therefore matches the changed builder's architecture, and its unconditional float attention-output setting does not depend on their differing dimensions or declared bfloat16 checkpoint dtype.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2232982c189b4c7cbb8bed6ee4953197",
              "call_bdae274e2db64f5381cb37def205eb0d",
              "call_4948132591654a62912b0f1b87189a83",
              "call_0f9cf575aeeb47bc8ab91885f97d65ca",
              "call_5f7a3fcce4674726b719bf6d57ff098a",
              "call_5c16deae6ae445e8a7386327c03db93f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The seven inspected Qwen configurations\u2014Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B, its FP8 and GPTQ-Int4 variants, Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B, and its Base, FP8 and GPTQ-Int4 variants\u2014each declare Qwen3MoeForCausalLM and match the changed builder. The float output setting is unconditional for each; their bfloat16 or float16 metadata does not parameterize this constructor argument. No dimensions or checkpoint-key mappings change.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_871df245bdbb417990b9b691b7fc9004",
              "call_215cff222cda413e8b7159925a95befa",
              "call_b52211ffbf30457b9d7125e1bfddf8b6",
